@* Why MIS: the question everyone asks a girl who reads, writes and paints *@
<section class="pursue-part career-why" id="why-mis" aria-labelledby="why-mis-heading">
    <div class="career-wrap why-wrap">
        <div>
            <p class="career-kicker">Why MIS</p>
            <h2 class="career-section-title" id="why-mis-heading">So why not English, Studio Art or Music?</h2>
            <p>I read constantly, I write, I love playing instruments, and I’ve been making art for as long as I can remember. And no, I’m not the next Ada Lovelace.</p>
            <p>But the more I made, the more I noticed technology was already inside everything I loved: the tools I draw with, the apps that put stories in my hands, the playlist that finds a song before I know I want it. Someone had to understand people to build those things well.</p>
            <p>That’s what MIS is to me. It’s the major for people who care as much about <em>why</em> someone uses a product as <em>how</em> it’s built. I didn’t leave the humanities behind. I brought them with me.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="why-quote">
            <blockquote>Technology is in everything. The best of it has a little poetry in it too.</blockquote>
            <ul class="why-loves" aria-label="What I bring with me">
                <li>Reading</li><li>Writing</li><li>Art</li><li>Music</li><li>Psychology</li>
            </ul>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>
